Rules for everything under `src/scene/` (rendered inside `<Canvas>`). Pairs with `react.mdc`.

## Scene Layout

```
src/scene/
├── index.tsx           # barrel: exports Scene only
├── Scene/              # Composition root: places every object, hotspot, light
├── CameraRig/          # Smoothly moves the camera to the active view
├── Hotspot/            # Clickable wrapper + floating DOM tag for a section
├── Lights/             # All scene lights
├── Decorations/        # Non-interactive floating extras
├── primitives/         # Reusable building blocks (Box, Ball)
└── objects/            # One directory per physical object (Cat, Desk, Monitor…)
```

- **Objects are placed at the origin.** An object component builds itself around `[0, 0, 0]` (its base on y = 0) and never sets its own world position. `Scene/index.tsx` positions it with a wrapping `<group>` or `<Hotspot>`. This keeps objects reusable and all layout in one file.
- `objects/` components are presentational. They may animate themselves with `useFrame`, but must not know about sections, selection or the camera.
- Interaction (hover, click, labels) belongs to `Hotspot`, not to objects.
- Large objects split private parts into sibling files (`Cat/CatHead.tsx`).
- Build shapes from `@/scene/primitives` (`Box`, `Ball`) where they fit; add a new primitive instead of copy-pasting the same mesh + material setup 3+ times.

## Colors And Numbers

- Every color comes from `PALETTE` in `@/configs`. Never write a hex string in a scene file; add a named palette entry.
- Camera views live in `configs/cameraViews.ts` (`HOME_VIEW`, `SECTION_VIEWS`). When moving a hotspot, update its view in the same change.
- Behaviour tuning values (speeds, angles, damping, segment counts) are named constants at the top of the file. Inline position/size/scale tuples for geometry are fine — they are the model itself.

## Adding A New Section (Hotspot)

1. Add a member to `ENUM_SECTION` in `src/types/section.ts`.
2. Fix every TypeScript error that follows — each `Record<ENUM_SECTION, …>` must get an entry:
   - `content/sections.ts` (label + emoji)
   - `configs/cameraViews.ts` (camera view)
   - `components/Panel/index.tsx` (panel content component, in a new `Panel/<Name>Content.tsx`)
3. Create the object in `scene/objects/<Name>/index.tsx` and export it from `scene/objects/index.tsx`.
4. Place it in `Scene/index.tsx` inside a `<Hotspot id={ENUM_SECTION.X}>`.
5. Add any new text to `src/content/`.

## Performance (useFrame)

- **Never allocate inside `useFrame`**: no `new Vector3()`, `.clone()`, array/object literals for math. Create scratch objects once with `useRef` (see `CameraRig`); the React Compiler lint rules reject mutating `useMemo` values. Enforced by `@react-three/no-new-in-loop` and `no-clone-in-loop`.
- **Never call `setState` inside `useFrame`.** Mutate refs (`ref.current.rotation.y = …`) instead.
- Guard refs: `if (!ref.current) return;` — refs are typed `useRef<Group>(null)`.
- Make motion frame-rate independent: use `delta` with `MathUtils.damp` or `1 - Math.pow(k, delta)`, and `clock.elapsedTime` for periodic motion. Never assume 60 fps.
- Keep geometry segment counts modest (≤ 48); the scene targets phones.
- Only meshes that visibly need it get `castShadow` / `receiveShadow`.
- Do not add more shadow-casting lights; there is one `directionalLight` in `Lights/`.
- Use `meshBasicMaterial` + `toneMapped={false}` for flat "glowing" surfaces (screens, sky); `meshStandardMaterial` for lit surfaces.

## Events

- Pointer handlers on 3D groups call `event.stopPropagation()` so overlapping hotspots do not both fire.
- Type them with `ThreeEvent<MouseEvent>` / `ThreeEvent<PointerEvent>` from `@react-three/fiber`.
- Use drei's `useCursor` for hover cursors; do not touch `document.body.style` directly.

## Models And Assets

- Prefer primitives. If a real model is needed, place a compressed `.glb` (Draco / `gltf-transform`, ideally < 2 MB) in `public/models/` and load it with ``useGLTF(`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}models/<name>.glb`)`` in its own `objects/<Name>/` component. Call `useGLTF.preload` at module scope.
- Everything that suspends (models, textures) must stay under the `<Suspense>` boundary in `App.tsx`.

## Imports

- Import three.js members by name (`import { Vector3, type Group } from 'three'`), not `import * as THREE`.
- Keep `@react-three/fiber` at v8 and `@react-three/drei` at v9 while on React 18.
